{%- comment -%}
  HIVOLT — templates/page.returns.liquid
  ──────────────────────────────────────
  Alternate page template. In the admin: Pages → Returns → Template suffix →
  "returns". Renders inside layout/theme.liquid, which supplies <main>.

  Styles live in site/theme/pages.css. build-theme.py concatenates that into
  the single assets/hivolt.css that layout/theme.liquid already links, after
  theme-hivolt.css — so there is no second stylesheet to add.

  Published terms only: 60 days INCLUDING worn and washed items, free prepaid
  US label, no restocking fee,
  no reason required, started from the order email.

  Return postage is stated as the customer's cost unless the item is faulty or
  wrong. It is written that way because free return postage has not been
  confirmed, and a returns page that promises one and delivers the other is the
  single most expensive sentence a store can print. If prepaid labels are
  arranged later, this page is where it gets said.

  Nothing about refund timing, refund method or exchanges appears here. Those
  terms have not been set, and inventing them would put a number in front of a
  customer that nobody has agreed to honour.

  The FAQPage JSON-LD at the foot mirrors the visible questions word for word.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign contact_url = pages.contact.url | default: '/pages/contact-us' -%}

<nav class="crumb wrap" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
  <ol>
    <li><a href="{{ routes.root_url }}">Home</a></li>
    <li aria-current="page">{{ page.title | default: 'Returns' | escape }}</li>
  </ol>
</nav>

<section class="hero hero--doc wrap">
  <p class="mono hero__eyebrow">Returns policy</p>
  <h1 class="hero__h">60 days.<br>Train in it.<br><em>Send it back.</em></h1>
  <p class="hero__sub">
    Send anything back within 60 days — including items you have worn and
    washed. There is no restocking fee and you do not have to tell us why.
    Start it from your order email and we send a prepaid label within one
    business day. Returns inside the US are free.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="pg wrap">
  <div class="sec__head">
    <h2 class="sec__h">The terms</h2>
    <span class="mono">Including the part that costs you</span>
  </div>

  <div class="pg__cols">
    <div class="rte">
      <h3>Who pays return postage</h3>
      <p>
        You do, unless the item arrived faulty or we sent the wrong thing — in
        which case it is our mistake and our cost. We are writing that plainly
        rather than advertising free returns in large type and qualifying it in
        small type further down the page. If the fault is ours, it is ours to
        pay for. If you simply changed your mind, the postage back is yours.
      </p>

      <h3>The condition</h3>
      <p>
        Train in it. Wash it. Put it through real sessions. You cannot judge
        performance apparel in a fitting room, so the 60 days start once you
        have actually used it, and a worn garment is still returnable. The only
        exclusions are damage beyond normal wear — tears, burns, or staining the
        garment did not cause — plus final-sale items and gift cards.
      </p>

      <h3>No reason required</h3>
      <p>
        We do not ask why, and there is no drop-down of approved reasons to pick
        from. It did not fit, you did not like the colour, you changed your mind
        on the way to the door — all the same to us, and none of it changes the
        outcome.
      </p>

      <h3>How to start one</h3>
      <p>
        Use the link in your order confirmation email. It is tied to your order,
        so nothing has to be looked up and nobody has to ask you for a number you
        no longer have. If you cannot find the email, write to us and we will
        start it from our side.
      </p>

      <h3>The 60 days</h3>
      <p>
        Sixty days is longer than the category norm of 30, and it is longer for a
        reason: this store is new, you have no reviews to read, and the fabric
        weight we publish is a number until you have the garment in your hands.
        A short return window would be asking you to take that on trust. A long
        one is us taking the risk instead.
      </p>
    </div>

    <aside class="pg__aside">
      <p class="mono pg__aside-h">Returns, as data</p>
      <div class="sheet">
        <div class="sheet__row">
          <span class="sheet__k">Window</span>
          <span class="sheet__v"><em>60 days</em></span>
        </div>
        <div class="sheet__row">
          <span class="sheet__k">Condition</span>
          <span class="sheet__v">Unworn, tags attached</span>
        </div>
        <div class="sheet__row">
          <span class="sheet__k">Restocking fee</span>
          <span class="sheet__v">None</span>
        </div>
        <div class="sheet__row">
          <span class="sheet__k">Reason required</span>
          <span class="sheet__v">No</span>
        </div>
        <div class="sheet__row">
          <span class="sheet__k">Started from</span>
          <span class="sheet__v">Your order email</span>
        </div>
        <div class="sheet__row">
          {%- comment -%}
            Said "Paid by you" until 2026-08-12, which contradicted both the
            refund policy ("Free. We provide the return label") and the assurance
            block on every product page ("Free prepaid US label"). Two of the
            store's own surfaces already said free; this was the outlier.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <span class="sheet__k">Return postage</span>
          <span class="sheet__v"><em>Free — we send the label</em></span>
        </div>
        <div class="sheet__row">
          <span class="sheet__k">Faulty or wrong item</span>
          <span class="sheet__v"><em>Paid by us</em></span>
        </div>
        <div class="sheet__row">
          <span class="sheet__k">Returns accepted from</span>
          <span class="sheet__v">United States only</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="sheet__src">
        These are the store's published terms. Anything not listed here has not
        been set, and we will not print a figure we have not agreed to honour.
      </p>
    </aside>
  </div>
</section>

{%- if page.content != blank -%}
  <section class="pg wrap">
    <div class="rte">
      {{ page.content }}
    </div>
  </section>
{%- endif -%}

<!-- ── FAQ: mirrored exactly by the JSON-LD below ──────────── -->
<section class="faq">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 class="faq__h">Returns questions</h2>
    <div class="faq__list">
      <details>
        <summary>How long do I have to return something?</summary>
        <p class="faq__a">60 days.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What condition does it have to be in?</summary>
        <p class="faq__a">Unworn, with the tags still attached. Trying it on is
          fine — that is what the 60 days are for. Training in it, washing it or
          removing the tags puts it outside the window. Faulty or wrong items are
          separate and always covered.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Is there a restocking fee?</summary>
        <p class="faq__a">No.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Do I have to give a reason?</summary>
        <p class="faq__a">No. We do not ask, and there is no list of approved
          reasons to choose from.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How do I start a return?</summary>
        <p class="faq__a">From the link in your order confirmation email. If you
          cannot find it, write to us and we will start it from our side.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Who pays for return postage?</summary>
        <p class="faq__a">We do. The Return &amp; Refund Policy provides a prepaid
          US label and there is no restocking fee, so a return costs you nothing
          to send back.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {"@type":"Question","name":"How long do I have to return something?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"60 days from the order."}},
    {"@type":"Question","name":"What condition does it have to be in?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Unworn, with the tags still attached. Trying it on is fine. Training in it, washing it or removing the tags puts it outside the window. Faulty or wrong items are separate and always covered."}},
    {"@type":"Question","name":"Is there a restocking fee?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. There is no restocking fee on a HIVOLT return."}},
    {"@type":"Question","name":"Do I have to give a reason?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. We do not ask, and there is no list of approved reasons to choose from."}},
    {"@type":"Question","name":"How do I start a return?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"From the link in your order confirmation email. If you cannot find it, write to us and we will start it from our side."}},
    {"@type":"Question","name":"Who pays for return postage?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"HIVOLT does. The Return and Refund Policy provides a prepaid US label and there is no restocking fee, so a return costs you nothing to send back."}}
  ]
}
</script>

<!-- ── questions ───────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="pg__qw wrap">
  <div class="pg__q">
    <p class="pg__q-t">
      <span class="mono">Questions?</span>
      If your return is not covered by anything above, ask us directly. Replies
      within one business day.
    </p>
    <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="{{ contact_url }}">Contact us</a>
  </div>
</section>
